{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1503889-storypath-momentum-questions","id":1503889,"title":"[Storypath] Momentum questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","General Onyx Path Discussion","Storypath System"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-25T06:44:45-08:00","id":1503889,"title":"[Storypath] Momentum questions","content":"So I got to run few game sessions in Scion 2E and Trinity Continuum - and Momentum questions are a bit returning, here and there. As we finally have Storypath subforum, let's collect all the problems and solutions. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> 1. <b>How much Momentum is generated by Failed and how much Botched roll?</b><br /> <br /> In <b>Scion Origin</b>, p. 70 we have this list:<br /> <br /> Consolation from a failed roll: 1<br /> \u2022 Failed Specialty: +1<br /> \u2022 Botch: +2<br /> <br /> So, if I read it correctly - normal roll Failure grants 1 Momentum to pool, Botch grants 3 Momentum?<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Characters always can declare to Botch roll</b>, before anything is rolled - for story reasons and/or generating Momentum?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T09:11:31-08:00","id":1503894,"title":"","content":"For Scion:<br /> <br /> 1. That's right. The base point of Momentum is the standard Consolation for a failure. In some cases, the Storyguide may offer a different Consolation instead, typically a promising narrative opportunity or a small Enhancement to a different future action. The extra Momentum from failing a specialty-based roll or from botching are not Consolations; they're always Momentum. (A botch always uses the Momentum Consolation, so it's always 3 Momentum, or 4 Momentum if you botch a roll using a specialty.)<br /> <br /> 2. Properly speaking, the Storyguide is the one who extends the offer to make a failure into a botch, and the player simply chooses whether or not to take the offer. The player can definitely ask the Storyguide &quot;hey, could I make this into a botch?&quot; but it's the Storyguide who decides whether they have an idea for the botch that merits the offer.<br /> <br /> There are subtle but significant differences between the Storypath Systems used by Scion and by the Trinity Continuum. If I'm looking at the Trinity corebook right, there a botch is simply a flat 2 Momentum rather than adding it onto the base Consolation. I'm not sure if Trinity has botch offers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 02-25-2023, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}